From ef5c9c60d2000f31c98064770947fddfd35d64aa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Juan Manuel Reategui Solis <reateguisolisjm@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 30 Jun 2026 18:32:26 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] PhoneApp: disable proximity screen-off during calls (MT6575
 workaround)

The LGE proximity sensor on MT6575 requires NVRAM calibration data that
is absent after a clean flash.  Without calibration the sensor reports
near indefinitely, locking the screen during calls with no way to hang up,
switch to speakerphone, or end the call.

Force screenOnImmediately=true so the PROXIMITY_SCREEN_OFF_WAKE_LOCK is
never acquired and the screen is always released immediately on call end.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: Ic103dbcda389e9d2a55325b23883e92205c5d1ab
---
 src/com/android/phone/PhoneApp.java | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/com/android/phone/PhoneApp.java b/src/com/android/phone/PhoneApp.java
index e7bc04e9..708120f2 100644
--- a/src/com/android/phone/PhoneApp.java
+++ b/src/com/android/phone/PhoneApp.java
@@ -1317,6 +1317,12 @@ public class PhoneApp extends Application implements AccelerometerListener.Orien
                             || PhoneUtils.isSpeakerOn(this)
                             || (!keepOn && (mBtHandsfree != null) && mBtHandsfree.isAudioOn())
                             || mIsHardKeyboardOpen);
+                // MT6575: proximity sensor requires NVRAM calibration data that is absent
+                // after a clean flash.  Without calibration the sensor reports "near"
+                // indefinitely, locking the screen during calls with no way to hang up.
+                // Force screenOnImmediately so the proximity wakelock is never acquired
+                // and the screen is always released immediately when the call ends.
+                screenOnImmediately = true;
 
                 // We do not keep the screen off when the user is outside in-call screen and we are
                 // horizontal, but we do not force it on when we become horizontal until the
